# Application Restart Log Marker

 When the Unimacs application starts, it writes a specific marker to the log to indicate a new run:
`=== Application Started/Restarted ===`

## Guidelines for log analysis
1. When analyzing log files (e.g., using `Scripts/unimacs-logs.sh`), look for the `=== Application Started/Restarted ===` marker.
2. Ignore any log entries before the last occurrence of this marker if you only want to analyze the current run.
3. If modifying the startup sequence, ensure this marker is still printed.
